From 7ef18771c1e450d0d0ff6736bc3e0a83a5956a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upstream Contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:26:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(loaders): add MultiJail, XSTest and Global-MMLU loaders

Evaluating safety per language needs samples tagged by language, and there
is no loader for the multilingual sets people use for it.

Add ak.load_multijail, ak.load_xstest and ak.load_global_mmlu. Each returns
samples with task set to the language, so per_task_deltas() reports every
metric per language. Translations of one item share metadata["group"], so
splits and paired tests can keep them together.

Each loader defaults to a pinned dataset revision and records it on the
sample, as load_bfcl does. load_xstest reads only the prompt file, because
the other five splits of that repo hold model completions.

The datasets import stays lazy, so the core keeps no required dependencies.
